      "text": "The factor is the average of the two low-prior-return portfolios minus the average of the two high-prior-return portfolios, using the value-weighted returns from the first (monthly) table in the file. The script parses only that table, treats -99.99 and -999 as missing, and drops any month where the factor cannot be computed.\n\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nSRC = \"6_Portfolios_ME_Prior_1_0.csv\"\nOUT = \"output.csv\"\nMISSING_VALUES = (-99.99, -999.0)\n\n\ndef is_missing(x):\n    return any(np.isclose(x, m) for m in MISSING_VALUES)\n\n\ndef main():\n    with open(SRC, encoding=\"latin-1\") as fh:\n        lines = fh.read().splitlines()\n\n    # Locate the column header of the first (value-weighted, monthly) table.\n    header_idx = None\n    for i, line in enumerate(lines):\n        parts = [p.strip() for p in line.split(\",\")]\n        if len(parts) > 1 and parts[0] == \"\" and any(\"PRIOR\" in p for p in parts[1:]):\n            header_idx = i\n            break\n    if header_idx is None:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Could not find column header line\")\n\n    cols = [p.strip() for p in lines[header_idx].split(\",\")][1:]\n    ncols = len(cols)\n\n    # Read contiguous block of monthly rows (YYYYMM dates) right after the header.\n    records = []\n    started = False\n    for line in lines[header_idx + 1:]:\n        if line.strip() == \"\":\n            if started:\n                break\n            continue\n        parts = [p.strip() for p in line.split(\",\")]\n        date_str = parts[0]\n        is_monthly = len(date_str) == 6 and date_str.isdigit()\n        if not is_monthly:\n            if started:\n                break\n            continue\n        started = True\n        vals = []\n        for p in parts[1:1 + ncols]:\n            try:\n                v = float(p)\n            except ValueError:\n                v = np.nan\n            if not np.isnan(v) and is_missing(v):\n                v = np.nan\n            vals.append(v)\n        while len(vals) < ncols:\n            vals.append(np.nan)\n        records.append([int(date_str)] + vals)\n\n    df = pd.DataFrame(records, columns=[\"date\"] + cols)\n\n    lo_cols = [c for c in cols if \"LoPRIOR\" in c]\n    hi_cols = [c for c in cols if \"HiPRIOR\" in c]\n\n    # ST_Rev = 0.5*(SMALL Lo + BIG Lo) - 0.5*(SMALL Hi + BIG Hi)\n    lo_avg = df[lo_cols].mean(axis=1, skipna=False)\n    hi_avg = df[hi_cols].mean(axis=1, skipna=False)\n    df[\"value\"] = lo_avg - hi_avg\n\n    out = df[[\"date\", \"value\"]].dropna(subset=[\"value\"]).copy()\n    out[\"date\"] = out[\"date\"].astype(int)\n    out.to_csv(OUT, index=False, columns=[\"date\", \"value\"])\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
